        "id": "1-1",
        "text": "**Linux, By Definition:**\n\nLinux (/\u02c8l\u026an\u0259ks/ (listen) LIN-\u0259ks) is a family of free and open-source software operating\nsystems based on the Linux kernel, an operating system kernel first released on September 17,\n1991 by Linus Torvalds. Linux is typically packaged in a Linux distribution (or distro for short).\n\n-Wikipedia\n\nThe above definition is probably not going to help you much if you don't know what an Operating\nsystem is, and what this UNIX thing is, so let's start at the first major point: What is an Operating\nsystem? I promise I won't make it boring!\n\n\n-----",
